  "query_preview": "(Friday through Monday)...\nSimilar to the track density forecasts immediately pre-development\nfor what became Hurricane Karina, ensemble members of the GFS and\nCanadian models have once again been the northern and eastern \noutliers with the track of newly-formed Tropical Storm Marie. \n\nThe two Google AI ensembles and the EC AI ensemble are once again\nfarther to the south and west with the core of the greater track \ndensity, moving Marie toward the west-northwest toward 22N/123W, \nthen on a track toward the west along 22N, with only a few \nensemble members deviating to the north of the core of greater \ntrack density. The 00Z GEFS has shown a substantial shift to the \nsouth and west with the greater track density toward those other\nensembles, though with a smaller number of ensemble members still\ntracking across northern Baja.\n\nThe most likely scenario for southern California from the current\nguidance would be for some mid and high level moisture from a \nstrengthening Hurricane Marie, well to the southwest of the area, \nto be drawn northeastward across southern California into the \nGreat Basin by the low pressure system off the West Coast. This \nwould bring a chance of showers and a slight chance of \nthunderstorms.\n\nOver the next day or so, there should be some narrowing in the \nspread of potential solutions across southern California as there\nis better model initialization of the area around strengthening\nTropical Storm Marie as well as some improvement in the forecast \nof the low pressure system just off the West Coast.",
